+// tileRowMaxCrossings is the capacity of one screen row's list of sight-polygon edge crossings
+// (sorted X coordinates; pairs [arr[2k], arr[2k+1]) are the visible spans of the row).
+//
+// The original engine used 32. A row crosses the sight polygon once per edge, and the polygon can have
+// up to sightPointsMax (1024) points, so long jagged sight edges (e.g. a level forest edge seen side-on)
+// exceed 32 easily: the extra crossings were dropped (wrong fog of war on that row) and sub_4C5500 then
+// read past the end of the array and panicked. 256 covers any realistic view at ~2.4 MB for the HD build.
+const tileRowMaxCrossings = 256
+
